  "explanation": "The question asks for the establishment date of the 'Cross of Liberty'. The source documents present three distinct entities or conflicting claims regarding this title:\n1. **Estonian Cross of Liberty**: Document D1S1/D2S1 states it was established on **24 February 1919**. Document D3S1/D4S1 states it was established on **12 March 1920**. These represent conflicting assertions for the same entity (Estonia), both of which are explicitly supported by the text.\n2. **Finnish Order of the Cross of Liberty**: Document D5S3 states the 'Order of the Cross of Liberty' (distinct from the Estonian medal, though sharing a name) was founded on **March 4, 1918**.\n\nPer the instruction to preserve distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers, and to treat all provided dates as fallible but potentially valid depending on the specific referent intended (Estonia vs. Finland, or conflicting records for Estonia), all three dates are included. The 'March 4, 1918' date refers to the Finnish order, while the other two refer to the Estonian decoration with conflicting historical records in the source."
